Step-1: Understanding Problem Statement
Publisher and Subscriber System => Design a message broker where publishers publish messages to topics and subscribers subscribe to topics. Every subscriber of a topic receives every message in order, and tracks its own read position (offset).

Step-2: Requirement Gathering
1. Publisher can send message
2. Subscriber can read message.
3. Subscriber and Publisher have indirectly many-to-many relation.
4. Publisher and Subscriber will be loosely coupled.
5. Subscriber can subscribe/unsubscribe to a Topic through the Broker; publishers stay unaware of subscribers.
6. Message read by Subscriber is near real-time.
7. Publisher can register and unregister themself to topic present on Broker.

Step-3: Clarify Requirements // In Clarify Requirements Step, you ask how the system should behave in edge cases.You don't solve them there. {State your assumption, and write down the expected behaviour}
1. At-least-once delivery
2. Order within topic guranted & not across Publisher

Step-4: Class Diagram + Relationship b/w Entities + Design Patterns

****Class-Diagram****

class Topic {
	-String id
	-String name
	-List<Message> messages
	-long latestOffset = -1
}

class Broker {
	attributes:
	-String id
	-String name
	-Map<String, Map<String, Subscription>> subscriptions; // topicId -> subscriberId -> Subscription
	-Map<String, Set<Publisher>> topicPublisher //key = topic_id, Topic Wise Publisher
	-Map<String, Topic> topics

	methods:
	addSubscriber(topicId, subscriber)
	removeSubscriber(topicId, subscriber)
	read(topicId, subscriber)
	write(topicId, payload, publisher)
}

class Publisher {
	attributes:
	-String id
	-String name
	-Broker broker

	methods:
	send(topicId, payload)
}

interface MessageListenser {
	+onMessage(String mesaage);
}
class Subscriber implements MessageListenser{
	attributes:
	-String id
	-String name
	-Broker broker

	methods:
	read(topicId)
	subscribe(topicId)
	unsubscribe(topicId)
	onMessage(String mesaage) // Broker calls this message.
}

class Subscription {
	-Topic topic
	-MessageListenser subscriber
	-long lastCommittedOffset = -1
}

class Message {
	-String id
	-String payload
	-Topic topic
	-long offset
}

****Relationship-b/w-Entities****
Topic - Broker = M:1
Subscription - Broker = M:1
Publisher - Broker = M:1
Subscriber - Broker = M:1
Message - Topic = M:1
Topic - Subscriber = M:M
Topic - Publisher = M:M
Subscription - Topic = M:1
Subscription - Subscriber = M:1

****Design-Patterns****
Observer Design Pattern and Facade Desing Pattern
Broker is the Facade and Observer subject
Subscriber is the Observer

Step-5: Schema Design + Attributes (PK + FK + attrib) + Cardinalities

****Cardinalities****
topics - brokers = M:1
publishers - brokers = M:1
subscribers - brokers = M:1
messages - topics = M:1
topics - subscribers = M:M
topics - publishers = M:M
topic_subscription - subscribers = M:1
topic_subscription - topics = M:1

****Schema Desgin + Attributes (PK + FK + attrib) ****

topics(	id String PK,
		String name,
		latestOffset long,
		broker_id String FK -> broker(id)
	)

brokers(	id String PK,
		String name
		)

publishers(id String PK,
			String name,
			broker_id String  FK -> broker(id)
		)

subscribers(	id String PK,
			String name,
			broker_id String FK -> broker(id)
		)

messages( id String PK,
		String payload,
		offset long,
		String topic_id FK -> topic(id)
	)

topic_publisher(	topic_id String FK -> topic(id),
					publisher_id String FK -> publisher(id),
					Primary key{ topic_id, publisher_id }
				)

topic_subscription(	topic_id String FK -> topic(id),
					subscriber_id String FK -> subscriber(id),
					last_committed_offset long,
					Primary Key{ topic_id, subscriber_id }
				)

